          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json; charset=utf-8",
            "text": "{\"about\":{\"description\":\"Does horror serve to uphold, or undermine, morality? Why do we find immoral acts we would reject in real life so fascinating? Is an abuse of power by regular people or otherworldly evil the ultimate horror? Arguably the most indulgent, exploitative and paradoxical of genres, horror cinema has long been concerned with exploring our most enduring assumptions on morality and what it means to be human.\\n\\nJoin us at Conway Hall for a screening of Robert Wiene’s mysterious and striking film **The Cabinet of Dr. Caligari** (1920), a seminal work which throws deeper questions of the complexity of moral responsibility and what the horror genre unveils about human nature.\\n\\n*At a local carnival in a small German town, hypnotist Dr. Caligari (Werner Kraus) presents the somnambulist Cesare (Conrad Veidt), who can purportedly predict the future of curious fairgoers. But at night, the doctor wakes Cesare from his sleep to enact his evil bidding. A monument of the silent film era and often considered one of the earliest examples of horror in cinema, The Cabinet of Dr. Caligari remains a thrilling and innovative work well over a century after its release.*\\n\\nThis screening is part of *Thinking in Frames*, a series exploring the big philosophical questions provoked by cinema and will be followed by an interactive discussion unpacking the film’s themes.\",\"one_liner\":null,\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"age_restriction\",\"title\":\"This is an all ages event. Under 16s must be accompanied by an adult.\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null},{\"type\":\"promoter\",\"title\":\"Presented by Conway Hall.\",\"subtitle\":null,\"external_link\":null}]},\"attendance_type\":\"live_only\",\"tty_to_extras\":[],\"streaming_options\":null,\"shopping_cart_enabled\":true,\"price\":{\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"amount\":null,\"sales_tax\":null,\"amount_from\":718},\"billing_promoter\":{\"id\":\"5578\",\"name\":\"Conway Hall\",\"image\":{\"url\":null},\"perm_name\":\"conway-hall-5nry\",\"profile_active\":false},\"unicorn\":true,\"marketeers\":[],\"max_tickets\":6,\"public_refund_policy\":{\"type\":\"cooling_off_enabled\",\"hours\":24},\"images\":{\"square\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-07-28/8536d178-49a2-40cc-964a-08aa2dfe7dbc.jpg?rect=328%2C0%2C844%2C844\",\"landscape\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-07-28/8536d178-49a2-40cc-964a-08aa2dfe7dbc.jpg?rect=47%2C0%2C1407%2C844\",\"portrait\":\"https://dice-media.imgix.net/attachments/2026-07-28/8536d178-49a2-40cc-964a-08aa2dfe7dbc.jpg?rect=518%2C0%2C464%2C844\"},\"name\":\"Thinking in Frames: Can Fear Be Moral?\",\"is_hidden_event\":false,\"social_links\":{\"event_share\":\"https://link.dice.fm/de889bc68de9?dice_id=de889bc68de9\",\"post_competition_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/b3b85197539e?dice_id=b3b85197539e\",\"post_purchase_extras_available_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/v268885d0fb2?dice_id=v268885d0fb2\",\"post_purchase_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/O252603f4b71?dice_id=O252603f4b71\",\"post_reminder_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/fb3f415819d8?dice_id=fb3f415819d8\",\"post_waitinglist_referral\":\"https://link.dice.fm/A37a733d368e?dice_id=A37a733d368e\"},\"acquisition_type\":\"purchase\",\"venues\":[{\"id\":\"3223\",\"name\":\"Conway Hall\",\"address\":\"25 Red Lion Square Holborn, London WC1R 4RL UK\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.51948760000001,\"lng\":-0.1168424},\"image\":null,\"city\":{\"id\":\"54d8a23438fe5d27d500001c\",\"name\":\"London\",\"location\":{\"lat\":51.507653,\"lng\":-0.107722,\"place\":\"Europe/London\"},\"country_code\":\"GB\",\"country_id\":\"GB\",\"country_name\":\"United Kingdom\"},\"perm_name\":\"conway-hall-obq5\",\"accessibility\":{\"url\":\"https://www.conwayhall.org.uk/about-us/faqs/\"},\"profile_active\":true,\"highlights\":[{\"type\":\"accessibility\",\"title\":\"Accessibility information\",\"external_link\":\"https://www.conwayhall.org.uk/about-us/faqs/\"}],\"space_name\":null,\"doors_open_date\":\"2026-10-30T18:00:00+00:00\",\"doors_close_date\":\"2026-10-30T20:30:00+00:00\"}],\"announcement_date_unix\":1785970800,\"is_fully_locked\":false,\"dates\":{\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"announcement_date\":\"2026-08-06T00:00:00+01:00\",\"sale_end_date\":\"2026-10-30T16:30:00+00:00\",\"sale_start_date\":\"2026-08-06T00:00:00+01:00\",\"event_start_date\":\"2026-10-30T18:30:00+00:00\",\"pre_sale_start_date\":null,\"event_end_date\":\"2026-10-30T20:30:00+00:00\",\"is_multi_days_event\":false},\"is_ticket_available_at_door\":false,\"tags_types\":[{\"name\":\"film\",\"value\":\"culture:film\",\"title\":\"Film\"}],\"seats_io_event_id\":null,\"perm_name\":\"53mvad-thinking-in-frames-can-fear-be-moral-30th-oct-conway-hall-london-tickets\",\"summary_lineup\":{\"top_artists\":[],\"total_artists\":0,\"total_free_texts\":4},\"unicorn_extras\":true,\"has_multiple_ticket_types\":true,\"multi_step_extras\":false,\"id\":\"6a6b63b620b4b40001e6328f\",\"seating\":null,\"presented_by\":\"Presented by Conway Hall.\",\"properties\":[],\"donation\":null,\"seats_io_public_key\":null,\"status\":\"on-sale\",\"date_unix\":1793385000,\"offers_extras\":false,\"secondary_status\":null,\"previews\":[],\"faqs\":[{\"id\":125349,\"title\":\"Further Information\",\"body\":\"This event is held in the Library, which is only accessible via stairs.\\n\\nIf you have any accessibility enquiries, please contact us at **info@conwayhall.org.uk** / **07442 405 055**.\",\"order\":0}]}",
